Subject: [PATCH 79/91] Nanite paste repairs, and fuel from more than one stack

Nanite paste:
- InitiateModuleRepair works now. The repair runs at the pilot's
  moduleRepairRate (10 hp a minute, +20% a level of Nanite Interfacing).
- Paste is used as the repair goes. A full repair costs the module's base price
  times shipBrokenModuleRepairCostMultiplier (0.5, -5% a level of Nanite
  Operation), paid in paste at its base price (6500). A 100k ISK module takes
  7-8 paste at level 0.
- Only repairs paid for with whole units of paste land, so stopping early keeps
  what was paid for.
- Refused for undamaged, burnt out or active modules, while anything is
  overloaded, and without paste in the cargo hold.
- Stops when the module is activated or damaged, something is overloaded, the
  paste runs out, or the pilot docks, jumps or leaves the ship.

Fuel:
- Modules that use fuel (cynos, siege, triage, jump portals, doomsdays) take it
  from every stack in the cargo hold, smallest first. Before, only one stack was
  used, and a short stack was deleted without the rest being taken.
